  <data>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="10" width="400" height="20">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(39,121,167,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>STOP 11 / 11 - AUDIT</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="30" width="848" height="34">
      <content textType="title" fontSize="24" fontFamily="Inter" bold="true" color="rgba(15,36,64,1)" wrap="false" textAlign="left">
        <p>Audit: guards, logs, and metrics agree</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <line startX="56" startY="64" endX="904" endY="64">
      <border color="rgb(39, 121, 167)" width="2"/>
    </line>
    <shape type="rect" topLeftX="56" topLeftY="84" width="532" height="384">
      <fill>
        <fillColor color="rgba(247,249,251,1)"/>
      </fill>
      <border color="rgb(214, 222, 232)" width="1"/>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="72" topLeftY="100" width="504" height="352">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="11" fontFamily="Roboto Mono" color="rgba(61,74,92,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.32" textAlign="left">
        <p>if (payment.getStatus() == PaymentStatus.INIT) {</p>
        <p>  throw new IllegalStateException("still INIT");</p>
        <p>}</p>
        <p>auditLogger.info("Payment processed: id={},</p>
        <p>    status={}", payment.getId(),</p>
        <p>    payment.getStatus());</p>
        <p>metrics.counter("payments.processed")</p>
        <p>    .increment();</p>
        <p>if (replay) {</p>
        <p>  metrics.counter("payments.replayed")</p>
        <p>      .increment();</p>
        <p>}</p>
        <p>// Prometheus: /actuator/prometheus</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="604" topLeftY="92" width="300" height="250">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13.5" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(61,74,92,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.4" textAlign="left">
        <ul>
          <li><p>The terminal guard: audit fires only on Authorized / Declined - an INIT payment is never counted as processed.</p></li>
          <li><p>Logs and metrics are driven by the same state transition - observability cannot lie.</p></li>
          <li><p>payments.processed / payments.replayed - replay is visible, not hidden.</p></li>
          <li><p>Failures threw earlier, so these counters stay clean.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="rect" topLeftX="604" topLeftY="360" width="300" height="108">
      <fill>
        <fillColor color="rgba(232,241,247,1)"/>
      </fill>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="616" topLeftY="374" width="276" height="84">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(15,36,64,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.35" textAlign="left">
        <p>Why it matters: a dashboard that counts "unknown" as "processed" is worse than no dashboard.</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
    <shape type="text" topLeftX="856" topLeftY="510" width="48" height="18">
      <content textType="caption" fontSize="12" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(138,148,166,1)" textAlign="right" wrap="false">
        <p>17 / 24</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
  </data>
  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>The last stop is audit, and it is where observability is designed in rather than bolted on. First a guard: if the payment is still INIT, we throw - because an unknown result must never be counted as processed. Then we write the audit log and increment Prometheus counters, including a dedicated replay counter so retries are visible. Because every failure path throws before this node, the metrics only ever reflect terminal, truthful states.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
